# Checkpoints 2 and 4 — parallel-beam redundancy, and the sign convention.
#
# Geometry of the test. A ring bar sits at phantom-frame angle phi and radius
# 60 mm; the ray's perpendicular offset from it is
#
#     d(phi) = | 60 * sin(phi + theta)  -  t |
#
# so a bar is cut dead centre whenever 60*sin(phi + theta) = t. At |t| = 60 mm
# that picks out exactly ONE bar and nothing else — the central aluminium bar is
# 60 mm off the ray and the baseplate is 75 mm below it in z. Steel bars sit at
# phi = 0, 120, 240 deg (radius 10 mm); poly at 60, 180, 300 deg (radius 15 mm).
#
# CHECKPOINT 4 — the sign table. Each run isolates one bar, and which MATERIAL
# it is depends on the sign convention:
#
#     theta     t        bar cut     material   chord    expect T ~
#     +30 deg  +60 mm    phi =  60   poly       30 mm      0.79
#     -30 deg  +60 mm    phi = 120   steel      20 mm      0.32
#     +30 deg  -60 mm    phi = 240   steel      20 mm      0.32
#     -30 deg  -60 mm    phi = 300   poly       30 mm      0.79
#
# A factor of 2.5 between poly and steel, so this is unmissable. Getting the
# pattern backwards means theta and t disagree in sign.
#
# HONEST LIMIT: a simultaneous flip of BOTH signs is undetectable with the
# current phantoms — pipe, bars and slab are all mirror-symmetric about the beam
# axis, so (theta, t) -> (-theta, -t) is an exact symmetry of the object. The
# relative sign is what is measurable; the absolute convention is fixed by
# [[Coordinate Conventions]] and ADR 0005, and only bites from Phase 3 on.
#
# CHECKPOINT 2 — redundancy. For a parallel beam, p(theta, t) = p(theta+180, -t)
# (NOT p(theta+180, t) — the detector coordinate reverses, and assuming
# otherwise is exactly how a sinogram ends up flipped). The last pair below is
# the same physical line as the first run, so it must agree within statistics.

/run/verbose      0
/event/verbose    0
/tracking/verbose 0

/cttwin/phantom bars
/run/initialize

# --- checkpoint 4: the sign table ---
/cttwin/scan/angle        30 deg
/cttwin/scan/translation  60 mm
/run/beamOn 100000

/cttwin/scan/angle       -30 deg
/cttwin/scan/translation  60 mm
/run/beamOn 100000

/cttwin/scan/angle        30 deg
/cttwin/scan/translation -60 mm
/run/beamOn 100000

/cttwin/scan/angle       -30 deg
/cttwin/scan/translation -60 mm
/run/beamOn 100000

# --- checkpoint 2: p(30, +60) must equal p(210, -60) ---
/cttwin/scan/angle       210 deg
/cttwin/scan/translation -60 mm
/run/beamOn 100000
